{
  "name": "duplicate-daemon",
  "integration": "portainer",
  "description": "REGRESSION LOCK for duplicate foreign ids when two Portainer environments front one Docker daemon. This is a real configuration and it was found by a real container: a host registered once as a local socket entry and again through the Portainer agent shows up twice in /api/endpoints, and both /docker/info calls return the SAME daemon ID. Every id this integration mints -- the host, its containers, its swarm nodes -- is scoped on that daemon ID, so the run emitted docker:<host>:host:bea7c305-... twice, differing only in the portainer.endpoint_id attribute. The unique_ids invariant catches it.\n\nThe resolution is to emit one asset per DAEMON, not per environment: two environments reading the same Docker socket are two paths to one machine, and giving them distinct ids would create two permanent assets for it -- two foreign ids from one integration can never merge back onto each other. The second environment is skipped whole, which also removes the duplicate container and swarm-node ids that came with it. Environment 1 wins because it is enumerated first, and the log names both so the fold is visible rather than silent.\n\nEnvironment 3 is a genuinely different daemon and must still be collected, which is what proves the dedup keys on the daemon ID rather than merely stopping after the first environment.",
  "kwargs": {
    "url": "$BASE",
    "mode": "portainer",
    "api_key": "ptr_fixtureAPIKeyValue0000000000000000000000=",
    "import_containers": "routable-only",
    "import_published_ports": "false"
  },
  "routes": [
    {
      "name": "endpoints",
      "match": {"method": "GET", "path": "/api/endpoints"},
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 200,
          "json": [
            {
              "Id": 1,
              "Name": "docker-hq-local",
              "Type": 1,
              "ContainerEngine": "docker",
              "URL": "tcp://192.0.2.40:2375",
              "GroupId": 1,
              "Status": 1,
              "Snapshots": []
            },
            {
              "Id": 2,
              "Name": "docker-hq-agent",
              "Type": 2,
              "ContainerEngine": "docker",
              "URL": "tcp://192.0.2.40:9001",
              "GroupId": 1,
              "Status": 1,
              "Snapshots": []
            },
            {
              "Id": 3,
              "Name": "docker-branch",
              "Type": 2,
              "ContainerEngine": "docker",
              "URL": "tcp://192.0.2.50:9001",
              "GroupId": 1,
              "Status": 1,
              "Snapshots": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "when_exhausted": "empty"
    },
    {
